# Schema Governance — Master Index

## Three-Layer Model

Every schema in this system belongs to exactly one layer:

| Layer | Repo | What Goes Here |
|---|---|---|
| **UAC External** | `unified-api-contracts/unified_api_contracts_external/<venue>/schemas.py` | Raw venue API request/response models |
| **UAC Canonical** | `unified-api-contracts/unified_api_contracts/unified_normalised_contracts/` | Cross-venue normalized outputs (CanonicalTrade, CanonicalOrder, etc.) |
| **UIC** | `unified-internal-contracts/unified_internal_contracts/` | Internal messaging, pub-sub, domain output shapes, shared identifiers |
| **Service-local** | `<service>/schemas/output_schemas.py` (SchemaDefinition only) or internal DTOs | Parquet write descriptors and HTTP DTOs never used outside the service |

CODEX: `02-data/schema-governance.md`

## Decision Tree (Quick Reference)

```
Parses an external API response (venue, data provider)?
  YES → UAC external: unified_api_contracts_external/<venue>/schemas.py
  NO  → Is it a canonical normalized output of the normalization pipeline?
    YES → UAC canonical: unified_normalised_contracts/
    NO  → Is it used in internal messaging, pub-sub, or cross-service?
      YES → UIC: relevant domain module or domain/<service-name>/
      NO  → Is it a SchemaDefinition / ColumnSchema (parquet infrastructure)?
        YES → Service-local: schemas/output_schemas.py
        NO  → Service-local HTTP DTO used only in this service?
          YES → CORRECT-LOCAL
          NO  → UIC (err toward centralizing)
```

